1
00:04:39,310 --> 00:04:45,310
Fearless lives forever.

2
00:09:18,620 --> 00:09:24,620
Bohemian Rhapsody is a music, drama film directed by Bryan Singer.

3
00:13:57,931 --> 00:14:03,931
Singer Freddie Mercury, guitarist Brian May, drummer Roger Taylor and bass guitarist John Deacon
take the music world by storm when they form the rock 'n' roll band Queen in 1970.

4
00:18:37,241 --> 00:18:43,241
Hit songs become instant classics.

5
00:23:16,551 --> 00:23:22,551
When Mercury's increasingly wild lifestyle starts to spiral out of control, Queen soon faces its
greatest challenge yet – finding a way to keep the band together amid the success and excess.

6
00:27:55,862 --> 00:28:01,862
Freddie Mercury, played by Rami Malek.

7
00:32:35,172 --> 00:32:41,172
Brian May, played by Gwilym Lee.

8
00:37:14,482 --> 00:37:20,482
Roger Taylor, played by Ben Hardy.

9
00:41:53,793 --> 00:41:59,793
John Deacon, played by Joseph Mazzello.

10
00:46:33,103 --> 00:46:39,103
Mary Austin, played by Lucy Boynton.

11
00:51:12,413 --> 00:51:18,413
John Reid, played by Aidan Gillen.

12
00:55:51,724 --> 00:55:57,724
Bohemian Rhapsody is a 2018 biographical drama film that focuses on the life of Freddie Mercury, the lead singer of the British rock
band Queen, from the formation of the band in 1970 to their 1985 Live Aid performance at the original Wembley Stadium.

13
01:00:31,034 --> 01:00:37,034
It was directed by Bryan Singer from a screenplay by Anthony McCarten,
and produced by Graham King and Queen manager Jim Beach.

14
01:05:10,344 --> 01:05:16,344
It stars Rami Malek as Mercury, with Lucy Boynton, Gwilym Lee, Ben Hardy, Joe Mazzello,
Aidan Gillen, Allen Leech, Tom Hollander, and Mike Myers in supporting roles.

15
01:09:49,655 --> 01:09:55,655
Queen members Brian May and Roger Taylor also served as consultants.

16
01:14:28,965 --> 01:14:34,965
A British-American venture, it was produced by 20th Century Fox, Regency
Enterprises, GK Films and Queen Films, and was distributed by Fox.

17
01:19:08,275 --> 01:19:14,275
The film was announced in late 2010, with Sacha Baron Cohen set to play Mercury.

18
01:23:47,586 --> 01:23:53,586
After he left the project in mid-2013 following creative differences with
producers, the project languished until Malek was cast in November 2016.

19
01:28:26,896 --> 01:28:32,896
Singer served as director through most of principal photography, which began in London in September 2017,
but was fired in December 2017 due to frequent absences and clashes with the cast and crew.

20
01:33:06,206 --> 01:33:12,206
Dexter Fletcher, who was originally set to direct when the project was early in development, was hired to complete the film; Singer
retained sole director credit as per Directors Guild of America guidelines, while Fletcher received an executive producer credit.

21
01:37:45,517 --> 01:37:51,517
Filming concluded in January 2018.

22
01:42:24,827 --> 01:42:30,827
Bohemian Rhapsody premiered at the Wembley Arena on October 23, 2018, and was theatrically released in
the United Kingdom the next day and in the United States on 2 November, to mixed reviews.

23
01:47:04,137 --> 01:47:10,137
While the musical sequences and Malek's performance were particularly praised, Singer's direction, the film's
portrayal of Mercury and other personnel, and its use of creative licence were criticized.

24
01:51:43,448 --> 01:51:49,448
However, it was well received by audiences and became a major box office success, grossing over $910.8 million worldwide on a production budget of $50–55
million, becoming the sixth-highest-grossing film of 2018 worldwide and setting the all-time box office records for the biographical and drama genres.

25
01:56:22,758 --> 01:56:28,758
Bohemian Rhapsody received numerous accolades, including a leading four wins at the 91st Academy Awards for Best Actor
(Malek), Best Film Editing, Best Sound Editing and Best Sound Mixing; it was also nominated for Best Picture.

26
02:01:02,068 --> 02:01:08,068
The film also won Best Motion Picture – Drama at the 76th Golden Globe Awards, and was nominated for the Producers Guild of America Award for Best
Theatrical Motion Picture and BAFTA Award for Best British Film, while Malek won the Golden Globe, Screen Actors Guild and BAFTA for Best Actor.

27
02:05:41,379 --> 02:05:47,379
The film explores themes of london, england, aids, musician, 1970s, biography.

28
02:10:20,689 --> 02:10:26,689
The tone is emotional.
